  "tagline": "Apache Jena's native RDF store, embeddable in Java or served over SPARQL with Fuseki.",
  "description": "TDB2 is the persistent triple store inside Apache Jena, the Java framework most semantic-web tooling is built on. It stores RDF in B+tree indexes on local disk with serializable transactions and can be used embedded in a JVM application or exposed as a SPARQL 1.1 endpoint through Fuseki. Jena adds rule-based inference, SHACL/ShEx validation, a GeoSPARQL module and Lucene-backed text search. It is free, standards-focused and dependable for single-machine datasets up to a few billion triples, but it does not cluster and bulk loading very large dumps takes patience.",
